 * `createIfAbsent` publishes with a hard-link no-replace primitive, so a concurrent creator's
-* file is preserved and this write is rejected with `FS_NOT_OBSERVED`; `existingDestination`
+* file is preserved and this write is rejected with `FS_NOT_OBSERVED`; when hard links are
+* unsupported, publication falls back to exclusive direct creation. The fallback exposes
+* bytes while writing; failures retain the target for inspection rather than risk deleting
+* a replacement by another writer. `existingDestination`
